base.prompt:
The target is closure of a discrete-generator subspace D in norm H. Three families approach chi as follows:
A. members of D, pointwise convergence only;
B. members of a larger subspace B, H-convergence;
C. members of D, H-convergence.
Which family establishes chi in the H-closure of D?
Answer with A, B, or C.

cosmetic_perturbation.prompt:
To prove v lies in the K-norm closure of S, consider:
A. K-convergent approximants from a larger space T;
B. approximants from S with weak convergence only;
C. K-convergent approximants from S.
Which family closes both obligations?
Answer with A, B, or C.

structural_perturbation.prompt:
The target is now the H-closure of the larger subspace B. The available families are:
A. members of D, pointwise convergence only;
B. members of B, H-convergence;
C. objects outside B, H-convergence.
Which family establishes the new target?
Answer with A, B, or C.
